WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.567
The takeaway is honest and useful: no current deep
learning model reliably predicts antibody

00:00:05.647 --> 00:00:08.329
fitness across all developability properties,

00:00:08.409 --> 00:00:14.590
so we are not yet at the point of trusting these
models to filter therapeutic candidates on their own.

00:00:14.670 --> 00:00:19.501
The good news is that intrinsic properties are
already captured reasonably well,

00:00:19.581 --> 00:00:22.754
which points toward the hardest remaining challenges.

00:00:22.834 --> 00:00:29.138
The authors argue the most promising path forward
is to enrich these models with structural information,

00:00:29.218 --> 00:00:31.716
antigen context, and physics-based priors,

00:00:31.796 --> 00:00:35.460
and to keep growing open antibody fitness datasets
like FLAb.
